      "summary": "caveman项目是一个针对Claude Code的提示工程技巧，通过模仿原始人说话方式（如用'few token'代替'few tokens'）大幅削减token用量，解决大模型交互中token消耗过高的问题。核心原理是利用语言模型对精简表达的理解能力，去除冗余词汇后仍能保持输出质量，减少65%的token，证明并非所有任务都需要详细提示。作为Claude Code的自定义技能使用，适用于代码生成、快速摘要等场景，能有效降低API费用或响应延迟，是一个既有趣又实用的效率实验。",
      "summary_en": "The caveman project is a minimalist prompt strategy for Claude Code that cuts token usage by 65% using caveman-like speech, addressing high LLM costs. It works by stripping unnecessary words while maintaining output quality, showing that many prompts are overengineered. Apply it as a custom skill for code generation or quick answers to reduce API bills or latency—a simple, practical experiment in prompt efficiency.",
